WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.455
A double-free defect happens when the same dynamically allocated object is released more than once.

2
00:00:06.455 --> 00:00:09.796
In C, that is usually not just a single mistaken call.

3
00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:21.110
It often reflects a deeper contract problem: more than one path believes it has cleanup authority, or ownership changed but the surrounding code did not update its assumptions.

4
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:29.312
These defects matter because dynamic memory is shared through pointers, structures, containers, callbacks, and error paths.

5
00:00:29.312 --> 00:00:35.007
A pointer value can be copied many times, but the allocation it refers to has one lifetime.

6
00:00:35.007 --> 00:00:41.993
When that lifetime ends, every remaining alias must stop acting as if the object is still valid or still owned.

7
00:00:41.993 --> 00:00:45.486
Double-free risk appears in normal engineering work.

8
00:00:45.486 --> 00:00:48.599
A function grows from one return path to several.

9
00:00:48.599 --> 00:00:52.017
A partially initialized object adds another member.

10
00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:54.902
A helper starts taking ownership on success.

11
00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:58.699
A container insertion changes who releases a child object.

12
00:00:58.699 --> 00:01:04.091
Without explicit rules, cleanup logic can drift into duplicated release behavior.

13
00:01:04.091 --> 00:01:06.369
Prevention is a design discipline.

14
00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:15.253
Developers should be able to point to the owner, the transfer rule, the valid lifetime, the cleanup authority, and the state after failure.

15
00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:20.417
Reviewers should not have to infer those facts from a long chain of conditionals.

16
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:29.757
This course stays focused on defensive practice: ownership, lifetime, cleanup paths, API contracts, testing, and tool-supported validation.

17
00:01:29.757 --> 00:01:36.895
The goal is to make memory release behavior predictable enough that one allocation has one clear cleanup story.
